# Shell scripts and the Hermes/gateway configs are executed on Linux. Without
# this, a Windows checkout commits CRLF and the server gets `\r`-terminated
# lines, which bash reports as a bogus "no such file or directory" on the
# shebang. Force LF regardless of the platform that wrote them.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
